------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Universal Commerce Protocol — Node.js reference implementation
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`apps/store` is derived from the UCP Node.js server reference implementation:

    https://github.com/Universal-Commerce-Protocol/samples
    rest/nodejs

    Copyright 2026 UCP Authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Retrieved 2026-07-30. At that revision the upstream sample passed 28/28 of its
own tests with 0 reported vulnerabilities.

Modifications made by this project, relative to upstream:

  - The catalogue is seeded by `scripts/seed.ts` rather than shipped as committed
    `products.db` / `transactions.db` binaries. Upstream has no seeding code, so
    without this the storefront would start with an empty catalogue once `*.db`
    is gitignored.
  - `package.json` renamed to `@pay-agent/store` and joined to the pnpm
    workspace; `better-sqlite3` moved from ^9.4.3 to ^11.7.0 to match the rest of
    the workspace and avoid building the native module twice.
  - Further modifications for gift-card funding are described in `docs/DESIGN.md`
    and were made in commits after the vendoring commit, so `git log` shows
    precisely what diverges from upstream.

The full Apache License 2.0 text is in `LICENSE`.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Standards referenced but not vendored
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`visa/trusted-agent-protocol` is cited as a reference only. Its LICENSE.md binds
use to the Visa Developer Center Terms of Use and it is not open source, so no
code from it appears in this repository. Where HTTP message signing is
implemented, the normative source is RFC 9421 (IETF).
